# ─── هوش‌یار / Hooshiyar — environment variables ───
# This app is BYOK (Bring Your Own Key): users' API keys live only in their
# own browser (encrypted with AES-GCM in localStorage) and never reach the
# server or this repo. No secrets are required here.

# Prisma database location (server-side only).
# - Local dev / bare-metal: a relative or absolute file path
# - Docker: leave as below (matches the volume mount in docker-compose.yml)
DATABASE_URL=file:/app/db/custom.db

# ─── Optional: demo engine ───
# The built-in demo engine lets visitors try the app without their own key.
# It is auto-disabled when nothing below is configured — the UI then hides the
# demo card and shows BYOK only. Nothing here is required for a self-host.
#
# Pick ONE of the two backends. All values are read from the environment, so a
# secret never has to live in this repo.
#
# Option A — any OpenAI-compatible endpoint with a free tier:
#   Cloudflare Workers AI, SiliconFlow, DeepInfra, Groq, a self-hosted
#   gateway, etc. The app speaks OpenAI's streaming API directly.
DEMO_BASE_URL=
DEMO_API_KEY=
DEMO_MODEL=
# Human-readable label shown in the UI (optional):
DEMO_LABEL=
#
# Option B — the original z-ai host (only works where .z-ai-config exists):
# ZAI_BASE_URL=
# ZAI_API_KEY=
# ZAI_MODEL=glm-4-flash

